      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to calculate the floor value of the square root of each integer from 1 to 16 and sum these values.\n\nThe floor function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ rounds down a number to the nearest integer. For instance, $\\lfloor 2.3 \\rfloor = 2$ and $\\lfloor 5 \\rfloor = 5$.\n\nLet's list the integers from 1 to 16 and calculate the floor values of their square roots:\n\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1 \\rfloor = 1$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.414 \\rfloor = 1$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.732 \\rfloor = 1$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{4} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2 \\rfloor = 2$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{5} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.236 \\rfloor = 2$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{6} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.449 \\rfloor = 2$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{7} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.646 \\rfloor = 2$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{8} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.828 \\rfloor = 2$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.162 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.317 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.464 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{13} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.606 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{14} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.742 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{15} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.873 \\rfloor = 3$\n- $\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4$\n\nNow we sum these values:\n\n\\[\n1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 4 = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}.\n\\]\n\nNow let's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the sum of the floor values of the square roots from sqrt(1) to sqrt(16)\ntotal_sum = sum(math.isqrt(i) for i in range(1, 17))\n\nprint(total_sum)\n```",
